"""
hydra-publish -- Cross-post an archerships.com post to multiple platforms.
Posts may be essays, images, or videos (terminology directive 2026-08-13).

archerships.com is the source of truth. This script adapts the cover image
for each platform, calls the appropriate publisher script, and writes the
result back to the essay's published_at frontmatter field.

Usage:
  hydra-publish <post-slug> --platforms twitter-article,facebook,substack,nostr
  hydra-publish <post-slug> --all
  hydra-publish <post-slug> --platforms twitter-article --image cover.jpg
  hydra-publish <post-slug> --dry-run --all

The essay slug is the directory name under ~/av/doc/posts/, e.g.:
  2026-05-27-sovereign-x

Available platforms:
  twitter-article   Full essay as a Twitter Article
  facebook          Short post with title, intro, and link
  substack          Full essay as a Substack draft
  nostr             Short announcement note (kind 1)

Requirements:
  pip install pyyaml beautifulsoup4 pillow

After publishing, open the essay frontmatter and fill in the URL for each
platform entry that was recorded with an empty url field.

Chromium must be accessible (x-publisher.py auto-launches it with remote debugging):
"""

